Backport of Circle's USB gadget fix series from its develop branch (after
Step 51.1.1), with its follow-up fixes. The gadget sources in 51.1.1 are
identical to develop just before the series, so this is upstream's diff
(gadget files, 7f60f02d..ddab4c9c) unchanged:

- 1bcfb78d usbmidigadget: Reuse MIDI interface after reconfiguration (#720)
  Without it, a second enumeration (host reboot, replug while self-powered)
  fails the assertion in CUSBMIDIGadget::CreateDevice().
- 91f41c83 dwusbgadget: Complete bulk transfer cancellation before buffer reuse (#721)
  CancelTransfer() now NAKs and disables the endpoint and waits for the
  hardware before returning, so a canceled OUT transfer can't complete into
  the MIDI receive buffer after it has been re-armed.
- 829a8c55 dwusbgadget: Synchronize receive buffers after DMA completion (#722)
  Discards cache lines refilled while DMA owned the receive buffer, so
  received MIDI data is not read stale.
- d57d6c11 dwusbgadget: Retire EP0 transfers before reset recovery (#731)
  EP0 OUT is no longer disabled on reset (that could leave a delayed event
  for the next SETUP); an active EP0 IN transfer is cancelled before its
  FIFO is flushed.
- ef913e82 usbmidigadget: Retire transfers when reset follows suspend (#732)
  A reset from the suspended state (host warm reboot) now deactivates the
  endpoints, and the MIDI gadget cancels both directions on deactivation.

Drop this patch when Circle is updated past these commits.

